12	// single test runs, so no test in this package can resolve a store under the
13	// developer's real home.
14	//
15	// Isolation here is by convention: a test threads an EntireEnv whose four
16	// Plugin*Dir fields are t.TempDir()s, and resolveXDGDir returns those without
17	// consulting the environment. Nothing enforces the convention. Any path that
18	// reaches resolveXDGDir with an empty pluginDir and no XDG variable set falls
19	// through to os.UserHomeDir() and resolves under the REAL home — with no error,
20	// because the callers treat store creation as best-effort.
21	//
22	// That is not a hypothetical gap. Instrumenting the fallthrough to record a
23	// stack and running the package once produced 1,193 escapes from 77 test
24	// functions across 21 files, and left a real directory behind:
25	//
26	//	~/.local/share/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/local/cli-<hash>/sessions
27	//
28	// i.e. `go test ./internal/cli` writes a junk repository into the developer's
29	// actual brain store. The suite passes either way, so the convention can rot
30	// without anything reporting it.
31	//
32	// Pinning here rather than fixing 77 call sites is deliberate: a call-site fix
33	// holds only until the next test forgets, while this holds for every test in the
34	// package including ones not yet written.
35	//
36	// XDG rather than HOME, deliberately. resolveXDGDir consults the XDG variable
37	// BEFORE falling back to the home directory, so pinning these four closes the
38	// same escape — and leaves HOME alone. Repointing HOME also works, but it
39	// silently disables entities_live_e2e_test.go: that test feature-detects the
40	// real provider by running `entire graph capabilities`, which needs the user's
41	// own config, so a sandboxed HOME turns the package's one live end-to-end proof
42	// into a permanent skip. Closing a hole by disabling a test is not closing it.
43	func TestMain(m *testing.M) {
44		hostXDGDataHome = hostDataHome()
45		root, err := os.MkdirTemp("", "entire-brain-cli-test-xdg-")
46		if err != nil {
47			fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, "pin test XDG roots: %v\n", err)
48			os.Exit(1)
49		}
50		for _, key := range []string{"XDG_CONFIG_HOME", "XDG_DATA_HOME", "XDG_STATE_HOME", "XDG_CACHE_HOME"} {
51			if err := os.Setenv(key, filepath.Join(root, key)); err != nil {
52				fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, "pin %s: %v\n", key, err)
53				os.Exit(1)
54			}
55		}
56		code := m.Run()
57		_ = os.RemoveAll(root)
58		os.Exit(code)
59	}
